  "tldr": "Primitive continuous bijective cell mechanisms that generate fixed scalar conditional laws are rigid: each is the increasing quantile or its rank reflection, so an intrinsic graph-budgeted orientation field is derived rather than assumed. This characterization yields attained sharp conditional counterfactual hulls, a bounded-degree rational Boolean polynomial, exact integration-before-optimization at bounded causal factor-graph width, and a fully legal four-cell path witness with non-strict nesting; the zero-budget equality is retained only as the known sanity reduction to Tan, Chen, and Du (2026, Theorem 2). Stagewise conditional DKW bands place the true quantile system in a fully specified alternative-law fiber and give an honest outer projection for every fixed or data-selected budget. The central open question is a terminating common-rank refinement algorithm whose certified outer endpoints contract pointwise despite context switches, payoff discontinuities, and the conditioning denominator.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "Published bijective and monotone-equivalence results establish complete counterfactual agreement in their respective regimes, but they do not study a bounded context-orientation failure class or graph-TV sharp partial-identification envelopes; generic causal-bound solvers do not exploit shared continuous ranks; projection inference does not provide a finite contracting computation for reused inverse quantiles and conditional-payoff ratios.",
    "niche": "A primitive finite-grid scalar triangular class isolates a structured and empirically interpretable failure mode: continuous bijective mechanisms generating the fixed cell law have a derived binary orientation, with neighboring disagreements limited by an analyst-chosen graph budget.",
    "fill": "The project proves cellwise quantile-orientation rigidity from primitive continuous bijections and fixed pushforwards, derives the positive-budget global orientation fiber and attained sharp hull, validates the geometry on an explicit rational triangular witness, compiles the Boolean coefficient map, solves the width-indexed optimizer, and obtains simultaneous finite-sample coverage by projecting a fully typed alternative-law fiber. The zero-budget equality is only a supporting known consistency check, and a concrete certified common-rank projection remains the open question."
